parseReal is operation
parseReal purpose "strtod, as glibc reads text in the C locale: white space, a sign, then inf or infinity, nan or nan(chars), a hexadecimal number (0x, digits with a point, p and a power of two), or a decimal one (digits with a point, e and a power of ten), each read correctly rounded; HUGE_VAL with ERANGE past the largest double, ERANGE for a decimal number that reads as a subnormal or as 0 (and a hexadecimal one that does so inexactly); the end of what was read is stored at `endAt` unless it is the address 0, the text itself when nothing was"
